WEBVTT

NOTE preferences: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.334
Language, units, temperature
and number formatting.

V0-2
00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.310
These belong to you, not to the site.

V1a-1
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.158
Preferences is the last
entry in the settings rail.

V1a-2
00:00:16.258 --> 00:00:18.994
Preferences are stored
against your user account;

V1a-3
00:00:19.094 --> 00:00:23.060
the calculation settings on the other
tabs are stored against the site.

V1b-1
00:00:23.627 --> 00:00:27.758
Language, Temperature Scale and the
separator setting change only how things

V1b-2
00:00:27.858 --> 00:00:32.317
are presented. Units of Measure can change
suggestions, as the next step explains.

V2a-1
00:00:40.097 --> 00:00:44.329
The stored amounts are millimetres.
Switching to imperial shows them

V2a-2
00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:48.537
in inches, with two decimal places;
metric gets one decimal place.

V2b-1
00:00:49.097 --> 00:00:53.453
Check after switching. Changing Units
of Measure and saving in the same

V2b-2
00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:57.786
visit does not re-convert the amounts
already on the Calculation tab.

V2b-3
00:00:57.886 --> 00:01:01.505
They are saved as though they
were already in the new unit,

V2b-4
00:01:01.605 --> 00:01:06.267
which rescales them by 25.4. After a
unit change, save, then reopen Settings

V2b-5
00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:10.787
and check Max Amount and Lynx Reference
Amount before you push anything.

V3a-1
00:01:17.257 --> 00:01:21.502
Saving a new language re-applies
translations across the site without a

V3a-2
00:01:21.602 --> 00:01:26.327
reload, and refetches your user record
so the choice sticks on your next visit.

V3b-1
00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.875
Anything Spatial Adjust has no translation
for stays in English, and every language

V3b-2
00:01:31.975 --> 00:01:36.585
other than English has gaps. The tab
names in the settings rail, the Discard

V3b-3
00:01:36.685 --> 00:01:41.600
changes confirmation and the scan-data
banner are in English whatever you choose.

V4a-1
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:52.920
Temperature scale changes the
weather strip. The group and decimal

V4a-2
00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.555
separator changes how every number
on the screen is punctuated,

V4a-3
00:01:56.655 --> 00:01:59.237
which matters most in
the dense table columns.

V4b-1
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.151
The weather strip follows
your temperature scale,

V4b-2
00:02:02.251 --> 00:02:05.370
and amount fields on the Calculation
tab show the unit you chose.
